La copia di llama.cpp che si compila (feature/ai/.cache/cxx/llama-cpp-src) non ha una cartella .git,
quindi a ogni configurazione CMake common/CMakeLists.txt stampa un warning "Git repository not found"
per ogni ABI. Il build info lo genera comunque cmake/build-info.cmake dal repository del progetto,
in cui sta la copia, e l'app non lo usa: il messaggio passa da WARNING a STATUS. Applicata da feature/ai/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt; percorsi dalla root del
submodule third-party/llama-cpp.

diff --git a/common/CMakeLists.txt b/common/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ if(EXISTS "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/.git")
         message(WARNING "Git index not found in git repository.")
     endif()
 else()
-    message(WARNING "Git repository not found; to enable automatic generation of build info, make sure Git is installed and the project is a Git repository.")
+    message(STATUS "Git repository not found; to enable automatic generation of build info, make sure Git is installed and the project is a Git repository.")
 endif()

 set(TEMPLATE_FILE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/build-info.cpp.in")
